# Commit and push after each prompt

After each chat prompt from the user, if that prompt changed project files, commit those changes and push them to the tracked remote branch before the turn ends.

- Include every file the prompt changed. Leave out secrets (`.env`, credentials, tokens).
- Use a short commit message in the repo's existing style, focused on why the change exists.
- Push the current branch. Do not force-push.
- If the prompt changed nothing, do not create an empty commit.
- If the user explicitly says not to commit or not to push for that prompt, skip it.
